<title>POLAND: BRE, ADIG apply to clear three funds.</title>
<headline>BRE, ADIG apply to clear three funds.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Rozwoju Eksportu (BRE) and Germany's Allgemeine Deutsche Investment GmbH (ADIG), which jointly are to run a mutual fund company applied to the Polish Securities Commission to clear three funds, BRE said.</p>
<p>BRE said in a Tuesday statement they applied to clear a money-market fund, a balanced fund and an aggressive fund, but did not give details.</p>
<p>It said the funds' units would start selling in the end of third quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>ADIG, owned by Bayerische Vereinsbank AG and Commerzbank AG, will have 40 percent of the company and BRE will have 60 percent.</p>
<p>BRE and ADIG invested together 18 million German marks in the company.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
